<item>
            <title>[LU-20657] short_hostname() truncates IPv4 addresses, misfiling yaml entities</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20657</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;short_hostname() strips everything from the first period, which is&lt;br/&gt;
right for an FQDN and destructive for an IPv4 address:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    short_hostname() &lt;/p&gt;
{
            echo $(sed &quot;s/\..*//&quot; &amp;lt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt; $1)
    }

&lt;p&gt;    short_hostname 10.135.230.14  -&amp;gt;  10&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;yml_entities() in yaml.sh appends every facet entity to&lt;br/&gt;
$logdir/node.$(short_hostname $host).yml. When the facets are named by&lt;br/&gt;
IP - which is what h2name_or_ip requires for ${facet}failover_HOST, since&lt;br/&gt;
given a hostname it expands `hostname -I` to every ethernet address and&lt;br/&gt;
emits non-LNet NIDs - every role from every server lands in one file:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    node.10.yml:&lt;br/&gt;
        node_type: MGS      node_name: 10&lt;br/&gt;
        node_type: MDS 1    node_name: 10&lt;br/&gt;
        node_type: MDS 2    node_name: 10&lt;br/&gt;
        node_type: OST 1..4 node_name: 10&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That file has no Build:/Node: header, because the header is written by&lt;br/&gt;
yml_node() into node.&amp;lt;host&amp;gt;.yml under the untruncated name. So the run&lt;br/&gt;
produces a bare YAML sequence that a results store rejects, and the real&lt;br/&gt;
per-node files carry no entities at all - no roles for any server.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Entries are also duplicated: facet_passive_host is truncated to the same&lt;br/&gt;
&quot;10&quot;, so each role is written twice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: leave an IPv4 address alone. An address has no domain to strip.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducible on any configuration whose ${facet}_HOST values are IP&lt;br/&gt;
addresses rather than names.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
